			)
		)
		(uuid "4cb11350-e025-40c0-8f8c-3f21ed5fc2e1")
	)
	(text "Differential Amplifiers"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 223.012 26.162 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5482e2d1-ac25-4295-aab2-d05e547ab7b4")
	)
	(text "1st Order Filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 60.96 96.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6099138a-7c30-42bb-afe3-f3da9eef0256")
	)
	(text "The voltage divider uses fairly high resistance values in order to reduce the\nstatic power consumption of the circuit\n	I = 3.3V / (2 * 47 kOhm) = 35 uA\n	P = 35 uA * 3.3V = 0.115 mW\n\nThe Capacitor is used to filter out noise and ripple on the Supply Line. \nThis noise is likely already very small, because of the LDO usage, but this \nfilter reduces the dependency between the ADC input and \nVref, as expected in the error model used (Vref only influences the Reference \nVoltage of the ADC, but not the Input Voltage)\n\nThe Filter has the following Cutoff frequency (exact frequency is not important, \nbut it must have have a small enough cutoff in order to efficently filter \nhigh frequency noises that can come from other subsystems):\n	Req = 47kOhm / 2 = 23.5 kOhm\n	f_cutoff = 1 / (2*pi*Req*C) = 68 Hz"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.576 126.746 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "692acdf5-3800-417f-9491-b737387924bd")
	)
	(text "ADC MUX"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 347.472 27.178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
				(thickness 0.4572)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "72793628-d2f1-4d8c-8037-66356e703cc9")
	)
	(text "INA is a Subtractor with integrated balanced resistors, producing a differential \ngain of 0.5 (because it is INA500 version B)\n\nIts output is then computed as: V_out = (0.5 * (V_IN+ - V_IN-)) + V_ref\n\nV_ref volatge, as specified in the INA daatsheet, in directly connected to the internal \nresistors, and so it should be provided with a very high input impedance to avoid any \ninfluence on the resistive network (which is very sensitive of mismatches, to obtain \na good CMRR) \n\nIn practice, the V_ref voltage is generated by a simple Voltage Divider, but is connected \nto the INA's Vref pin via a Voltage Follower, to guarantee a that the voltage is\nfed to Vref pin with a very small impedance. \n\nThe Vref is generated once for each channel in order to reduce the total number \nof circuit components, and void to introduce additional mismatch source between the\ndifferential signals in each channel."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.576 104.902 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7d0f2483-25a0-4a49-9e8f-e97bb6ea07fc")
	)
	(text "(1 filter for each differential output channel of Sensor)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 93.98 29.718 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
		)
		(uuid "888d012a-11f4-4346-b680-c538c5ef1216")
	)
	(text "To be mounted ONLY \nin the case a 2nd order \nfilter is needed\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 83.82 198.628 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "96672cca-5fad-43dd-8dda-2a3e0573218e")
	)
	(text "Common Mode filter. \nCommon Mode filter Cap. should be at least 10 times smaller than \nthe Differential Cap. to avoid transforming the Common Mode\nsignal into Differential Signal (basically inducing error in \nthe real measurement) due to the Common Mode Cap. mismatch \n(due to tollerances)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 112.014 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ac01f392-70a5-4035-9017-10df5c31c7eb")
	)
